# Normalize to LF in repo; MSVC, CMake, Ninja, and Qt are all LF-clean.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts keep CRLF
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binaries
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# Fuzz corpora are BYTES, not text, and `* text=auto eol=lf` above would
# rewrite them. That is not a cosmetic problem: 85 of the current seeds contain
# a CR, several of them precisely because they exercise how the parser handles
# one, and normalising it away turns a seed that tests CR into a seed that does
# not — while the file still looks present, still counts toward the corpus, and
# still gets fed to the fuzzer. Silent loss of coverage is the worst failure a
# corpus can have, so the whole tree is marked binary.
tests/fuzz/seeds/** binary
tests/fuzz/seeds-telnet/** binary
tests/fuzz/regressions/** binary
